{"id":"solar-cell","title":"Solar cells: short-circuit current and open-circuit voltage","sections":[{"heading":"The idea","body_md":"A solar cell is a large pn junction that absorbs light. Each absorbed photon with enough energy makes an electron-hole pair. Minority carriers generated within about a diffusion length of the junction wander to it and are swept across by its field, so light adds a reverse current, the **photocurrent**, to the ordinary diode current.\n\nThe I-V curve is the diode curve shifted down by the short-circuit current \\(I_{sc}\\). Power comes out in the fourth quadrant, where the voltage is positive but the current is negative. Two numbers summarize the cell. \\(I_{sc}\\) is the current with the terminals shorted; \\(V_{oc}\\) is the voltage with them open, where the forward diode current exactly cancels the photocurrent. The best operating point, \\(P_{max}\\), lies at the knee between them.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Solar-cell I-V curve in the fourth quadrant: the current equals minus I_sc at zero volts and crosses zero at V_oc.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V_D</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">I_D</text><polyline points=\"50,161 52.2,161 54.5,161 56.8,161 59,161 61.2,161 63.5,161 65.8,161 68,161 70.2,161 72.5,161 74.8,161 77,161 79.2,161 81.5,161 83.8,161 86,161 88.2,161 90.5,161 92.8,161 95,161 97.2,161 99.5,161 101.8,161 104,161 106.2,161 108.5,161 110.8,161 113,161 115.2,161 117.5,161 119.8,161 122,161 124.2,161 126.5,161 128.8,161 131,161 133.2,161 135.5,161 137.8,161 140,161 142.2,161 144.5,161 146.8,161 149,161 151.2,161 153.5,161 155.8,161 158,161 160.2,161 162.5,161 164.8,161 167,161 169.2,161 171.5,161 173.8,161 176,161 178.2,161 180.5,161 182.8,161 185,161 187.2,161 189.5,161 191.8,161 194,161 196.2,161 198.5,161 200.8,161 203,161 205.2,161 207.5,161 209.8,161 212,161 214.3,161 216.5,160.9 218.8,160.9 221,160.9 223.2,160.9 225.5,160.9 227.8,160.8 230,160.8 232.2,160.7 234.5,160.7 236.8,160.6 239,160.5 241.2,160.4 243.5,160.2 245.8,160 248,159.8 250.3,159.5 252.5,159.1 254.8,158.7 257,158.1 259.2,157.4 261.5,156.6 263.8,155.5 266,154.2 268.2,152.6 270.5,150.5 272.8,148 275,144.9 277.2,141 279.5,136.2 281.8,130.3 284,122.9 286.2,113.7 288.5,102.4 290.8,88.3 293,70.8 295.2,49.1 297.5,26 299.8,26 302,26 304.2,26 306.5,26 308.8,26 311,26 313.3,26 315.5,26 317.8,26 320,26\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"86\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"></text><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"161\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"56\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">I_sc</text><circle cx=\"291.1\" cy=\"86\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"297.1\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V_oc</text></svg>","figure_alt":"Solar-cell I-V curve in the fourth quadrant: the current equals minus I_sc at zero volts and crosses zero at V_oc."},{"heading":"Key equations","body_md":"\\[ I_D = I_S\\left(e^{V/V_{th}} - 1\\right) - I_{sc} \\]\nUniform generation in the n region: \\(\\Delta p(\\infty) = G_L\\tau_p\\), \\(\\Delta p(0) = 0\\) at short circuit, so\n\\[ \\Delta p(x) = G_L\\tau_p\\left(1 - e^{-x/L_p}\\right), \\qquad I_{sc} = AqL_pG_L \\]\n\\[ V_{oc} = V_{th}\\ln\\frac{\\tau_pG_LN_D}{n_i^2} \\]","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Excess hole profile in an illuminated n region: zero at the junction edge and rising to G_L τ_p deep inside, with the rise over about one diffusion length.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">x / L_p</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Δp</text><polyline points=\"50,176 52.2,171.9 54.5,167.9 56.8,164.1 59,160.4 61.2,156.8 63.5,153.3 65.8,150 68,146.7 70.2,143.6 72.5,140.6 74.8,137.6 77,134.8 79.2,132 81.5,129.4 83.8,126.8 86,124.3 88.2,121.9 90.5,119.6 92.8,117.4 95,115.2 97.2,113.1 99.5,111 101.8,109.1 104,107.2 106.2,105.3 108.5,103.5 110.8,101.8 113,100.2 115.2,98.5 117.5,97 119.8,95.5 122,94 124.2,92.6 126.5,91.2 128.8,89.9 131,88.6 133.2,87.4 135.5,86.2 137.8,85.1 140,83.9 142.2,82.9 144.5,81.8 146.8,80.8 149,79.8 151.2,78.9 153.5,78 155.8,77.1 158,76.2 160.2,75.4 162.5,74.6 164.8,73.8 167,73.1 169.2,72.4 171.5,71.7 173.8,71 176,70.3 178.2,69.7 180.5,69.1 182.8,68.5 185,67.9 187.2,67.4 189.5,66.8 191.8,66.3 194,65.8 196.2,65.3 198.5,64.9 200.8,64.4 203,64 205.2,63.5 207.5,63.1 209.8,62.7 212,62.3 214.2,62 216.5,61.6 218.8,61.3 221,60.9 223.2,60.6 225.5,60.3 227.8,60 230,59.7 232.2,59.4 234.5,59.1 236.8,58.9 239,58.6 241.2,58.4 243.5,58.1 245.8,57.9 248,57.7 250.2,57.4 252.5,57.2 254.8,57 257,56.8 259.2,56.6 261.5,56.4 263.8,56.3 266,56.1 268.2,55.9 270.5,55.8 272.8,55.6 275,55.5 277.2,55.3 279.5,55.2 281.8,55 284,54.9 286.2,54.8 288.5,54.7 290.8,54.5 293,54.4 295.2,54.3 297.5,54.2 299.8,54.1 302,54 304.2,53.9 306.5,53.8 308.8,53.7 311,53.6 313.2,53.5 315.5,53.4 317.8,53.4 320,53.3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"322\" y=\"49.3\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Δp(x)</text><line x1=\"117.5\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"117.5\" y2=\"26\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"117.5\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">L_p</text><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"51\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"51\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">G_Lτ_p</text></svg>","figure_alt":"Excess hole profile in an illuminated n region: zero at the junction edge and rising to G_L τ_p deep inside, with the rise over about one diffusion length."},{"heading":"Worked example","body_md":"A cell has \\(L_p = 80\\ \\mu\\mathrm{m}\\), \\(\\tau_p = 5\\ \\mu\\mathrm{s}\\), \\(N_D = 5\\times10^{15}\\ \\mathrm{cm^{-3}}\\) and \\(G_L = 10^{19}\\ \\mathrm{cm^{-3}s^{-1}}\\):\n\\[ \\frac{I_{sc}}{A} = qL_pG_L = (1.602\\times10^{-19})(8\\times10^{-3})(10^{19}) \\approx 12.8\\ \\mathrm{mA/cm^2} \\]\n\\[ V_{oc} = 0.026\\ln\\frac{(5\\times10^{-6})(10^{19})(5\\times10^{15})}{10^{20}} = 0.026\\ln(2.5\\times10^{9}) \\approx 0.56\\ \\mathrm{V} \\]"},{"heading":"Common pitfalls","body_md":"- Calling power \"delivered\" in the first quadrant. A generator needs opposite signs of \\(V\\) and \\(I\\).\n- Using \\(G_L\\tau_p\\) as the boundary value at the junction. At short circuit it is zero.\n- Expecting \\(V_{oc}\\) to scale with light intensity. It grows only logarithmically; \\(I_{sc}\\) scales linearly.\n- Forgetting the cm conversion for \\(L_p\\)."},{"heading":"Where this leads","body_md":"Run the junction the other way, forward biased and in a direct-gap material, and recombination emits light: that is the LED. The small-signal resistance of the cell's diode is the same \\(V_{th}/I_D\\) you will meet in the diode model."}]}